WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.730
Ino's entered the Earth 
Science Olympiad by herself?

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.800
Yeah.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.230
She said the preliminaries are this Sunday.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.400
Wow.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.280
I'm surprised.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.480
I never thought she'd 
go for such a challenge.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.810
Right?

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.160
I wish I could have participated, too.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.620
It's really rare, since they only 
hold it once every four years!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.580
<b>Outcrop Bouldering</b>

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:26.790
I wonder what kinds of sports are 
in the Earth Science Olympiad.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.790
<b>Fossil Excavation Race</b>

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.790
<b>Telescope Focusing Race</b>

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.560
Sports? It's not a sports event.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.050
Huh? It's not?

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.630
But it's called an Olympiad, so I thought...

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.390
If you're curious about something, 
you should look it up first.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.120
<b>Japan Earth Science Olympiad Application</b>

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.590
The Earth Science Olympiad is an 
annual earth sciences competition for

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.060
<b>Earth Science 
Olympiad</b>

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.060
middle and high school students.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.520
The preliminary competitions 
are held domestically,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.990
and select winners go on to represent their 
nation in an international competition.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.110
You know a lot about it, Sakura-senpai.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.380
My little sister's participating.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:00.470
Little sister?

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.910
You have a little sister?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.800
She's in her last year of middle school.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.140
Wow, she's a middle schooler!

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.230
She wants to make it through 
the domestic competitions

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.860
and go to the international 
competition in Thailand.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.840
Thailand...

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.300
<b>Souvenir Request List 
Tom yum goong
 Thai curry 
Elephant goods
Muay thai</b>

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.300
Mira, Mira, you're jumping the gun.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.650
Still, I wonder why Ino's 
doing this all of a sudden.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.060
Apparently the idea came to her when she 
was looking at photos from our summer camp.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:28.350
I see. The display from the 
Geological Museum, huh?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:34.490
We're a small club, so I always thought 
stuff like that was a world away for us,

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.060
but there she is...

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.710
What?

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.250
Sakura-senpai, you have a really 
kind look on your face right now.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.300
What?!

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.750
I was complimenting you!

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.570
So what?!

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.390
08. Winter Diamond

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.980
<i>This must have been a river long ago.</i>

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.990
<i>I can look forward to exploring it later.</i>

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.030
<i>Today I'm representing 
the earth sciences club.</i>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.360
<i>I need to stay strong!</i>

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.790
<b>Japan Earth Science Olympiad
Test Hall</b>

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.750
<i>I-I'm so anxious...</i>

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.920
<i>There are so many participants.</i>

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.800
<i>They're all people from 
schools I don't know, too...</i>

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.340
Hey, neighbor!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.590
Good luck today!

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.470
Sorry...

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.680
You're funny.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:09.350
I'm Saeki.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.280
I'm Inose. Nice to meet you.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.890
Inose-chan, are you feeling really nervous?

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.250
Is this your first time?

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.320
Yes.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.190
I'm also the only one here from my school...

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:27.160
Plus, the thought that everyone here 
is a rival makes me feel alienated.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.810
Rival?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.800
I get it!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.770
I made it to the main 
competition last year.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:41.020
So, while I have no intention 
of losing to the others,

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.440
once you get them to open up,

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.890
they're all just people who couldn't be more 
enthusiastic about earth sciences, like us.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.440
Of course, some universities let you use your 
results in this competition to secure entry,

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.630
so there are some people 
participating just for that.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.900
Huh? That's an actual policy?

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.290
It was written in the application guidelines.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.440
R-Right...

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.170
<i>I shouldn't tell Monroe-senpai.</i>

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.370
Oh, looks like it's almost time.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.900
Well, let's just have fun with this, Inose-chan.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.120
R-Right!

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.520
Good morning, everyone.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.830
We'll be handing out your test sheets now.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.100
<i>Saeki-san's incredible. She's made it 
to the main competition before!</i>

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:24.670
<i>I'm sure she's really smart and
will fly through the questions.</i>

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.050
Now, please begin.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.730
<i>She looks like a predator that's spotted its prey!</i>

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.380
<i>Focus, focus.</i>

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.730
<i>First, I'll tackle the geology problems.</i>

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.740
<i>How to read a clinometer, the law 
of superposition, index fossils...</i>

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.910
<i>These problems are fun to solve.</i>

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.320
<i>There's a geologic map 
and volcanoes and magma!</i>

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.970
<i>Meteorology, oceanology, 
environmental science...</i>

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.250
<i>These are my worst subjects!</i>

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.520
<i>I've studied all of them a little,</i>

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.480
<i>but I don't think I solved those problems 
right since I don't understand how they work.</i>

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.930
<i>That just leaves astronomy...</i>

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.310
<i>Questions about the planets.</i>

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.890
<i>Huh? I'm solving these more
 easily than I expected.</i>

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.220
<i>Why?</i>

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.150
<i>It's because those two are 
always in the club room.</i>

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.530
You have ten minutes left.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.770
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.590
<i>There's just one question 
left that I don't understand.</i>

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.700
<i>The ones who finished early 
are already starting to leave.</i>

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.160
<i>"Choose two correct statements 
from the following, listed A to O."</i>

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.780
<i>A to O...</i>

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.130
<i>A to O...</i>

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.720
<i>A to... O?</i>

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.300
<i>Ao!</i>

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.220
Okay, time's up.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.700
Whew, it's over!

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.350
That was fun!

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.960
Good work, Inose-chan.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.080
Are you okay?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.310
I feel like I just released 
everything I'd crammed in...

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.280
But I'm glad I'm participated.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.320
There were a lot of things I felt 
for the first time by coming here.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.000
Yeah?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.510
Like just how small I am...

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:22.460
Oh, yeah?

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:27.560
Yeah. I realized the world is 
much bigger than I thought.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.070
<i>Oh. I thought she was 
talking about her height.</i>

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:33.900
Why don't we walk to the station 
together, since we're here?

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.920
Sure!

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.250
Oh, right, there's a place I wanted 
to stop by on the way home.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.560
Shopping?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.190
No.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.800
I discovered a path I believe 
was made by filling in a river,

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.820
so I wanted to explore it.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.890
What? That sounds fun!

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.830
I failed!

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.250
Huh? The results were already announced?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:58.410
No, I scored myself, and it was awful...

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.410
But you seem happy despite that.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:08.920
Yes. I learned there are lots more 
people like us outside of this club.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.180
Like us?

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.920
Oh, want to see pictures?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.800
I do, I do!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.370
She took a step forward and went for 
something bigger than we ever did.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:20.510
Yeah.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.810
Going home?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:22.270
Yeah.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.010
I feel better after seeing everyone.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:27.900
I need to give it another shot, too.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.910
Good luck.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.590
This is Saeki-san?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.110
Yeah!

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.910
This is a commemorative photo from when 
we went exploring on the way home.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.820
There's no blur in the digital camera!

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:40.930
Oh, Saeki-san took that one for us.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.340
Mine is...

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.970
Ta-da!

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.130
A hot plate?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.090
Yes.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.970
Since Endou-sensei said we 
couldn't have a portable stove,

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.390
we borrowed this from Araya-sensei!

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.020
Shall we start getting things set up?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.100
Yeah!

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:18.240
The culture clubs share a breaker!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.920
Be mindful.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.740
What's this? A mystery hot pot?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.160
No, a Christmas party.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.250
Would you like to join us?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.730
I appreciate it, but the newspaper 
club's having its own.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.140
Oh, that explains the outfit.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.130
Merry Christmas and Happy New Year!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.340
We got scolded.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.850
How embarrassing.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.680
But there's a terrible draft in here,
so we can't turn off the heater...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.600
Oh, I know.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.520
We could do a hot rock pot!

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.390
Hot rock?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:51.340
It's a primitive cooking method that uses
a stone heated to high temperatures

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.460
<b>Stone                      In!</b>

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.480
to cook food.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.330
I get it!

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.650
Okay, first...

00:09:55.650 --> 00:10:00.190
we'll have to go hunt down some dacitic tuff!

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.880
Huh? From where?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.710
The Oga Peninsula!

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.040
Denied!

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.500
Let's try talking to Ao!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.800
<b>Commemoration of Blowing the Breaker</b>

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:21.840
<i>Apparently we can't use the heater 
and the hot plate at the same time.</i>

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.150
<i>What do we do?</i>

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:29.950
<i>We could just prepare some 
blankets and not use the heater.</i>

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:33.460
<i>We could also make the hot pot 
a bit hotter and use that for heat.</i>

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>How about that?</i>

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.860
<b>Shedding scales</b>

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:44.330
<i>Honestly, Mira's always making me feel better.</i>

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.790
<i>I wish there was something 
I could do to thank her.</i>

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.510
Earth Sciences Club 
Christmas and
New Year Party!!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:11:00.340
Time to start the first earth sciences club 
Christmas and New Year hot pot party!

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.690
Thanks for inviting us.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:07.350
I never thought I'd get to 
eat hot pot in the club room.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.450
What is that sparkly thing?

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.520
Mira-chan lent it to me.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.380
It's a thermal blanket like the ones 
used on artificial satellites.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.800
I bought it when we visited JAXA!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.320
Oh, yeah, you bought a bunch of things.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:25.630
Wearing this makes me feel 
like an artificial satellite!

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:27.290
How does that feel, exactly?

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.210
It does look warm, though.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.950
I hope the hot pot tastes okay.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.690
M-Mira-chan!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.630
This hot pot is spicy!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.390
Huh? I only used store-bought kimchi, though.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:46.890
It's spicy!

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:47.940
Why?!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.060
U-Um, maybe because of this?

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.900
<b>Chili Peppers</b>

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.060
Chili peppers for added spiciness?

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:55.900
Did you...

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.610
Y-You told me to put 
everything in, so I thought...

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.260
Senpai! Please wait a 
moment before you eat it!

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.450
It has a nice punch that makes it delicious.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.300
It warms me up!

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.120
Huh?

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.390
Must be an adult's sense of taste?

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:15.190
So cold...

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.910
Mira, here's the key to the 
roof that you asked for.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.090
Oh, thank you!

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.280
The roof?

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.310
Yes!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:25.620
Once we're all warmed up, I thought 
we could all stargaze together.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.090
Oh, a kimchi hot pot! Nice!

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.250
I-It's spicy!

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:32.960
Huh?

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.270
But an adult's sense of taste...

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.790
We can see far and wide!

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.650
The sky is pretty, since it's cold out.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.360
That's the Winter Diamond, right?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:49.940
There's Sirius and Rigel and, uh...

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.780
Aldebaran and Capella.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.830
Pollux and Procyon.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.720
Sakura-senpai, you looked them up?

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:00.610
I just managed to remember a few 
because they're named after rocks.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.050
What are you laughing about?

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:03.600
Oh, right.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:09.000
If you add in Betelgeuse from Orion, 
you get the Great G.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.410
G? From the alphabet?

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:14.230
Yeah, you link those there.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:22.070
It's still strange to think a geology club
member like me is looking up at the sky.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:25.580
Are you still upset the clubs were merged?

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:29.360
If I was, I wouldn't have made this.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.830
Thanks.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.220
Everyone...

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.910
What is it?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.870
This is a present from us.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:38.500
Huh?

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.340
You can open it.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.250
Okay.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:45.890
It's an album!

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:52.210
I had Sakura-chan select and compile them 
from my collection of secret photos.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.530
There are scenes from our 
activities and our events...

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.030
You took this many?

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:12.410
It's incredible!

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.530
There were a lot of photos 
I would have felt bad including,

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.250
so it was hard work narrowing them down.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.180
Huh?

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:26.530
Ao?

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.590
Are you okay?

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:33.570
Huh? What's wrong?!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:36.150
Huh? Oh, sorry.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:38.480
I was just having so much fun...

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.160
Are you okay?

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.230
Yeah.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.720
The effect of the kimchi is running out.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:47.680
We'll water down the soup and make udon.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:52.640
Man, the cold really hits hard at my age.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.870
I don't know how you can 
all wear such short skirts.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.850
Heater, heater...

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.700
Ah, Sensei, you can't—

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.530
Huh?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:05.330
Sensei!

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:13.550
Even three days later, there are still a lot 
of people making their first shrine visit.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.000
Ino-senpai, is that...

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:16.960
A map!

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.330
I knew it!

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.430
No, I mean...

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.040
You have two?

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.600
There have been a lot of flood control 
improvements made to this area,

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:26.900
so I wanted to compare it to an older map.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.510
I see.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.650
This is the commemorative stone for 
the flood control construction!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.600
Let's take a picture!

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.840
Senpai, can we say our prayers first?

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.330
Oh, you're right. Sorry.

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:45.920
After we pray, we'll draw fortunes, 
then have dango at the tea shop...

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.800
I want to drink amazake, too!

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.470
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.470
<b>Natural Rock Fortunes</b>

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.470
<b>Fan Fortunes</b>

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:50.650
Are those...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.540
Fortunes with natural rocks!

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:55.600
<b>Natural Rock Fortunes</b>

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.600
I want to draw one!

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.690
I can't see it that well from here.

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:03.190
Based on the colors, I think those 
are crystals, onyx, and red jasper.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:06.150
Hey, we need to say our prayers!

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:14.400
May I discover an asteroid with Ao!

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.320
Y-You shouldn't shout it...

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:21.290
I heard it makes it easier for the gods 
to hear your wish if you say it out loud.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.860
Come on, Ao and Ino-senpai, say yours, too!

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.690
Can we go talk over there for a bit?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:39.310
Ao-san, I thought it was strange when 
you stayed home from school before.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:43.110
Is there something bothering you?

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:45.540
If you don't mind, I'd like to help.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.270
Please tell me whatever it is.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:53.140
The truth is, it's been decided that 
my dad's going to be transferred...

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:56.110
and I'm supposed to move away with him.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.180
Huh?

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:00.020
When are you moving?

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.640
In March. During spring break.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.540
No way...

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:08.500
But we promised to discover 
an asteroid together!

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.050
M-Mira-chan, calm down.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.290
B-But...

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.340
Ao-san is just as shocked as you are!

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:20.240
Let's just think about what we can do now.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:24.490
Ao-san, can you tell us more about the move?

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.860
E-Emergency meeting of 
the earth sciences club!

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.210
I'd like to gather lots of ideas,

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.360
so I've asked the newspaper club 
members to join us.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.280
A meeting right after opening 
ceremonies... This is rather sudden.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:45.160
You mentioned that Manaka's 
going to be moving.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.770
So our topic is her farewell party, right?

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.840
Goodbye, Manaka
Thanks for the dreams

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.090
I propose this title.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.840
No!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:57.180
<b>Topic</b>

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:57.180
How to support Ao-san 
and Mira-chan in
 achieving their goal

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:56.610
It might not be our place to speak up,
 since this is a family matter.

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:57.180
But...

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.490
You don't want these two to give up hope.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.600
Senpai...

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.140
So...

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.500
I'd like to get some ideas 
about how both of them

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:09.320
can participate in the club together 
even after Ao-san moves away.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.940
<i>I didn't even notice.</i>

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.630
<i>Ao was worrying about
 this all by herself, and I...</i>

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.680
<i>I'm a failure as a friend.</i>

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:16.530
Ow!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.190
Ouch!

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:20.770
Where's your usual spirit?

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:23.090
You should be throwing out 
ideas at times like this!

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:24.870
Learn from Monroe!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:28.560
She's busy studying for her exams, and
 I'm still getting message after message.

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:32.850
<i>She's right. This isn't the 
time to beat myself up.</i>

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.210
<i>I need to think.</i>

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.550
<i>How can Ao and I...</i>

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.570
<i>realize our dream?</i>

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.600
I'm sorry I'm late!

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:44.840
Suzu-san.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:45.910
Ao...

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:48.350
I can't believe you'd leave us like this.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.310
<b>Please don't look for us

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.900
Let's elope together!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.480
Wait! What about <i>our</i> dream?!

00:18:57.890 --> 00:18:59.740
If we can't elope,

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:02.490
how about one of us becomes 
a commuter wife on weekends?

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:05.950
She'll be four hours away by bullet train.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.200
That might not be an option due to the cost.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.680
Then why don't we camp out 
during the longer breaks

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:13.920
and have concentrated observation nights?

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.640
That sounds good.

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:19.590
Though that would be more of a personal 
activity than a club activity, I think...

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:23.550
Can you borrow telescopes and 
other equipment from the school?

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.680
They'd have to negotiate that,

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.600
and they'd be hard to haul there.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.940
How about I support her as a guardian?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.260
I plan on getting my driver's license, anyway.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.420
Um, why...

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:43.110
Why are you all putting so 
much thought into this for me?

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:47.170
Dummy.

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:49.960
It's because we like you, of course.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.040
That's right.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:57.090
Just last night, Sakura-senpai 
wouldn't stop messaging me!

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.210
Ino! You don't need to talk about that!

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:04.990
Still, it's hard to come up 
with the perfect solution.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:09.810
I suppose the most realistic one is you 
conducting your activities in different places.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.590
Yeah...

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:14.350
There are plenty of ways to stay in contact.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:15.910
Excuse me.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:17.180
That voice...

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.110
Onee-cha—

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:27.200
Company 
President

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.660
What's going on?

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:23.970
We were told to take home the personal 
belongings left in the council room.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:27.200
Misa-nee... what kind of role do
you play in the student council?

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:29.890
I heard about what's going on from Mira.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:34.670
Ao-kun, why don't you think about ways 
to avoid moving in the first place?

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:39.670
But her dad's transfer is 
already set in stone, right?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:43.090
Are you suggesting she throw a 
tantrum in front of her parents?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:44.150
Exactly.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.050
Huh? At her age?

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.380
Sorry.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:49.690
I don't mean that literally.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:54.020
Ao-kun, have you even told your parents
that you don't want to move?

00:20:55.280 --> 00:21:00.710
You haven't just accepted that it's 
already been decided, have you?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.180
I haven't told them how I feel.

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:10.300
The whims of a child aren't going 
to change the parents' situation.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.090
That's true.

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:18.880
But in that case, why not act like a child 
should and try putting up at least some fight?

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:23.350
Except you'll be doing it with a specific
 plan about how you'll live your life—

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:25.330
Misa-nee, um...

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.800
Could you make it easier to understand?

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.020
Hmm, well...

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.260
Fortunately, I'll be enrolling in 
a distant university next year.

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:39.280
Which means, starting this spring,
 I'll be living on my own.

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:40.770
So, Ao-kun,

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.580
you should live in my old room.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.020
In other words,

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:47.490
why don't you try proposing the idea 
of living with Mira to your parents?

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:50.870
Liv...

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.330
Living together?!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:58.870
<i>I had no idea what to do
 when I heard she was moving,</i>

00:21:58.870 --> 00:21:59.980
<i>but living together?</i>

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:03.950
<i>What's going to happen to us now?</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
09. 
True Feelings

00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:38.700
Next time, "True Feelings."
